# M B008 — skills/build-fix
1 CO WF-015~ GOV-014~ m=MN c=M | A test is updated only for an actually requested contract change: otherwise changing it to pass weakens verification (WF-015) or changes behavior beyond scope (GOV-014).
2 CO WF-015 m=MN | No assertion weakening, any-casts, disabled strict mode or suppressed template diagnostics to pass (WF-015).
3 CO WF-015 WF-008 GOV-014 | Restore to green without hiding failures, weakening behavior or unrelated changes.
4 CO WF-013~ c=M | Determining the authoritative contract for cross-stack failures is part of diagnosing the actual failure (WF-013).
5 CO WF-013 | Restates WF-013 (reproduce and diagnose before editing).
6 CO WF-013~ c=M | Deciding whether the defect is in code, setup, expectation, environment or an intended change is the diagnosis step of WF-013.
7 CO WF-013 | Fix root causes before downstream symptoms (WF-013).
8 CO WF-014 | Restates WF-014.
9 CO WF-014~ c=M | Not repeating variants of a failed guess is part of WF-014's bounded, focused iterations.
10 CO WF-015 m=MN | Restates WF-015.
11 CO GOV-014 RUN-009~ ARC-001~ m=M | Preserve architecture and conventions while fixing (GOV-014 behavior/scope, RUN-009 conventions, ARC-001).
12 CO WF-014~ WF-008~ c=M | Stop when progress stalls instead of speculative edits: bounded iteration (WF-014) and fixing until green or genuinely blocked (WF-008).
13 CO WF-007~ WF-014~ m=MN c=M | Do not run unrelated build systems merely because they exist (risk-scoped checks, focused verification).
14 CO WF-001~ c=M | Read the path-matched rules for the failing area before editing (WF-001 apply applicable rules; explicit read because path rules may not be loaded).
15 CO WF-013~ c=M | Determine the failing area before running commands (diagnosis of the actual failure).
16 CO WF-014 | Start with the narrowest reproducing command (WF-014).
17 CO WF-013~ WF-018~ DEP-014~ c=M | Use package.json scripts that exist and do not assume a test runner (Vitest baseline for new projects); WF-018 states the same for CI, and reproducing the actual failure (WF-013) requires the project's real commands.
18 CO WF-013 | Read complete output, group by root cause, fix the highest-leverage cause first (WF-013).
19 CO WF-013 WF-014 | Backend repair loop (reproduce, diagnose, inspect, smallest change, rerun, compare, expand).
20 CO ARC-001 WF-015~ m=MN | Never solve dependency-direction problems with invalid project references (ARC-001).
21 CO WF-013 WF-014 | Frontend repair loop (same steps).
22 CO WF-015 DEP-015~ FE-001~ DEP-001~ m=MN c=M | No any-casts, disabled strict mode, unexplained suppression, NgModule workarounds, speculative framework API replacement or extra libraries to bypass a local issue.
23 CO WF-013 WF-016~ c=M | Cross-stack contract failures: determine the authoritative contract, do not patch both sides inconsistently; generated clients regenerated from source (WF-016).
24 CO WF-013 WF-014 | Test-failure repair flow.
25 CO WF-015 GOV-014~ m=MN | No weakened assertions or deleted/skipped tests; intentional changes update the test after confirming they were requested.
26 CO WF-013~ c=M | After a dependency-related failure inspect version, compatibility, peers, diagnostics and migration docs before updating usage (diagnosis of the actual failure).
27 CO DEP-003~ DEP-002~ DEP-001~ DEP-006~ DEP-007~ DEP-025~ m=MN | Dependency changes during repair go through add-dependency; no package swaps to get green, no duplicated csproj versions, no force flags, no reflexive lockfile deletion.
28 XW m=MN c=M rel=WF-013,DEP-003 | 'Do not fabricate replacement APIs from memory when they can be verified': epistemic duty about API facts during upgrades; the oracle requires registry verification only for package versions (DEP-003).
  e: when the API cannot be verified
  s: During an upgrade the agent rewrites a call to an option API it remembers and the build passes but runtime behavior differs: no policy requires checking the documentation; M does.
29 CO WF-013~ GOV-014~ c=M | Framework-upgrade repair procedure; no additional unrelated upgrade (diagnosis, scope).
30 CO DEP-008~ WF-008~ WF-009~ m=MN c=M | Do not change the declared SDK/Node/framework/language version because the local machine differs; report an unresolvable toolchain limitation instead of editing source (platform decision DEP-008; blocked reporting WF-008/WF-009).
31 CO WF-008~ GOV-014~ c=M | Never leave the repository knowingly worse; unrelated pre-existing failures left alone unless blocking or requested.
32 CO WF-013~ | Distinguish source from local-toolchain failure (diagnosis).
33 CO WF-014 WF-008~ c=M | Bounded focused attempts with stop-and-reassess conditions; no repeated failed guesses.
34 CO WF-008~ GOV-014~ c=M | Revert or correct a fix introducing new unrelated failures; no unrelated cleanup unless blocking or requested.
35 CO ARC-001~ ARC-008~ ARC-011~ SEC-005~ FE-003~ WF-015~ m=MN | A build fix must not bypass architecture; a green build obtained by violating it is not a repair.
36 CO TST-010 c=M | A diagnostic probe or new behavioral test stays covered by maintained tests before the probe is removed (TST-010 via verify step 4); build/compiler commands need no tests.
37 CO WF-005~ WF-008~ WF-007~ WF-004~ c=M | Completion criteria of build-fix: affected scope green, consistent contract, no known regression, no accidental workaround; no unrelated builds.
38 CO WF-003~ m=M | Run verify for the final completion pass when appropriate (WF-003).
39 CO WF-009 | Report builds and tests as PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE (WF-009).
40 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-009 | Build-fix report fields Initial failure, Root cause, Changes made, Remaining issues: report format beyond WF-009's verification-state reporting.
  s: Agent reports the PASS/NOT RUN matrix only, without root cause and changes: WF-009 satisfied; M's output format requires the extra fields.
41 CO WF-009 WF-008~ m=MN | Do not claim the problem is fixed while a known relevant failure remains (WF-009 never imply an unchecked/failed area passed).
